{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13g2-bandgap -- `klt sim` request template for trim-coverage (issue #416, Part of #412): the trim-ladder range / resolution / linearity bench behind DR-0011's ratified Trim row, cited by DR-0014.",
    "One .op per (process, supply, temperature, trim code). The code rides `corners.params.trim_code` (a top-level .param in the body; klayout-tools #3035) -- the 11 codes of the primary 27 C grid are 11 corner units of ONE request. The supply and the .nodeset seeds are baked into a per-(process, supply, temperature) body variant, exactly as the PWL-ramp benches bake the supply, because the seeds differ per variant. The runner image's single-models.lib carries one process per request (klayout-tools#2668), so --batch writes one request per (process, supply) at 27 C (11 codes) plus two typ/3.30V step-temperature probes (-40 and 125 C, codes 128 and 129).",
    "Measurements are `expr` figures (an operating point has no .meas search); values arrive as `print` output at ngspice's default precision. dvsns_v and the closed-loop verdict are formed by sim/harness/trim_coverage_klt.py from the reported operands, the same practice the committed records use."
  ],
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "netlist": "@@BODY@@",
  "netlist_source": "schematic",
  "models": {
    "lib": "@@CORNER_BUNDLE@@"
  },
  "corners": {
    "process": [
      "typ"
    ],
    "temperature_c": [
      27
    ],
    "params": {
      "trim_code": [
        0,
        1,
        2,
        4,
        8,
        16,
        32,
        64,
        128,
        129,
        255
      ]
    }
  },
  "analysis": {
    "kind": "op",
    "args": ""
  },
  "measurements": [
    {
      "name": "fb_v",
      "expr": "v(fb)"
    },
    {
      "name": "sns1_v",
      "expr": "v(sns1)"
    },
    {
      "name": "sns2_v",
      "expr": "v(sns2)"
    },
    {
      "name": "vref_v",
      "expr": "v(vref)"
    },
    {
      "name": "det_v",
      "expr": "v(det)"
    },
    {
      "name": "vbeq3_v",
      "expr": "v(cb3)"
    },
    {
      "name": "i_mkfb_a",
      "expr": "i(vmkfb)"
    }
  ],
  "options": {
    "timeout_s": 900,
    "keep_artifacts": true
  }
}
